    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d514">

                <pb facs="0508" n="500" sameAs="frus:frus1941v03/pg500"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890G.00/570: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister Resident in Iraq</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Knabenshue</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Baghdad</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-04-16T17:00:00+03:00">April 16, 1941—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received April 17—9:31 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>84. British Ambassador’s recommendations as reported in my 75,<anchor n="32"
                        xml:id="d514-f1"/> have been approved by Cabinet and he will see Gailani
                    today. This might result in peaceful landing British troops especially in view
                    strength of accompanying naval units.</p>
                <p>It is possible my telegrams are not being sent and I therefore asked Ambassador
                    to request Foreign Office, London, to keep our Embassy informed.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Knabenshue</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
